Package: DStressR
Title: Differential Stress-Response Modeling for Chemical Genomics Screens
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Christian L.", family = "Müller", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "ch.mueller@lmu.de")
  )
Description: Model-based differential promoter activity analysis for
    high-throughput chemical genomics screens. DStressR constructs
    growth-adjusted luminescence responses, optionally calibrates them with
    matched empty-vector controls, estimates compound-wide and
    promoter-specific stress responses, moderates promoter-level uncertainty,
    adjusts for technical covariates, and ships public Escherichia coli
    reporter-perturbation data for reproducible examples.
URL: https://muellsen.github.io/DStressR/, https://github.com/muellsen/DStressR/
BugReports: https://github.com/muellsen/DStressR/issues
